Subject: compat fts: always FTS_NOCHDIR on VMS

The compat fts(3) saves and restores the working directory with
open(".") and fchdir(); VMS can open neither a directory nor fchdir to
one (NOTES N4). With FTS_NOCHDIR it walks by full path instead.

--- a/compats.c	2026-11-05 21:10:35.094245561 +0000
+++ b/compats.c	2026-11-05 21:10:35.157068280 +0000
@@ -2269,6 +2269,10 @@
 		return (NULL);
 	sp->fts_compar = compar;
 	sp->fts_options = options;
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* No open(".") or fchdir() on VMS: always walk by full path. */
+	sp->fts_options |= FTS_NOCHDIR;
+#endif
 
 	/* Logical walks turn on NOCHDIR; symbolic links are too hard. */
 	if (FTS_ISSET(FTS_LOGICAL))
